You're so happy that you cried?

279
00:20:15,520 --> 00:20:16,880
Oh, uh...

280
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:19,930
They left me behind as
the only single person now.

281
00:20:19,950 --> 00:20:21,450
Oh, I'm proud, then.

282
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:22,180
Right.

283
00:20:23,170 --> 00:20:24,370
- Shouldn't you feel sorry, Dad?
- Dad!

284
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:26,320
Oh, just kidding.

285
00:20:28,630 --> 00:20:30,830
Congratulations, Sarm and Mr. Jam.

286
00:20:31,790 --> 00:20:32,740
Thank you.

287
00:20:32,770 --> 00:20:33,810
- Thank you.
- Thank you, everyone.

288
00:20:33,830 --> 00:20:34,500
Mm.

289
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:39,230
Getting to the good part now?

290
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:42,430
I'll stay outside.

291
00:20:45,230 --> 00:20:46,090
Come on.

292
00:20:46,130 --> 00:20:46,880
Let's leave them to it

293
00:20:47,030 --> 00:20:48,530
- so that they can enjoy the moment,
- Right.

294
00:20:48,650 --> 00:20:49,220
shall we?

295
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:49,970
Okay.

296
00:20:49,990 --> 00:20:51,090
- Let's go.
- Follow me, sons.

297
00:20:51,110 --> 00:20:51,940
Bye-bye, everyone.

298
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,940
- Come on, let's go.
- Make sure you break the bed.

299
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:55,630
Bye-bye, everybody.

300
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:20,040
Thank you

301
00:21:20,930 --> 00:21:21,840
for choosing me.

302
00:21:25,580 --> 00:21:27,320
You were not a choice I made.

303
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:30,130
You were a discovery.

304
00:21:31,830 --> 00:21:33,090
Oh, Jam...

305
00:21:42,430 --> 00:21:44,230
I will tear you to shreds.

306
00:21:47,670 --> 00:21:49,610
You never take anything seriously.

307
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:53,030
I'm serious.

308
00:21:53,450 --> 00:22:00,620
[One month later]

309
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:23,020
Sarm...

310
00:22:26,930 --> 00:22:28,280
Sarm...

311
00:22:31,690 --> 00:22:33,210
Sarm.

312
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:34,920
I can kiss you all day, you know?

313
00:22:38,250 --> 00:22:39,290
Sarm.

314
00:22:39,310 --> 00:22:39,940
Hm?

315
00:22:40,020 --> 00:22:42,050
I need to go to work.

316
00:22:42,700 --> 00:22:43,600
Little Jam,

317
00:22:43,620 --> 00:22:44,620
today's Saturday.

318
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:48,190
I am heading to the shop.

319
00:22:48,210 --> 00:22:49,650
New items come in today.

320
00:22:53,590 --> 00:22:54,350
Okay.

321
00:22:55,230 --> 00:22:56,030
If that's the case,

322
00:22:56,050 --> 00:22:57,770
I'll join you at lunch

323
00:22:58,480 --> 00:23:00,320
so that we can have a good time
at a different place.

324
00:23:02,060 --> 00:23:04,130
Having lunch at a different place?

325
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:05,690
No.

326
00:23:05,710 --> 00:23:06,750
A different place

327
00:23:06,770 --> 00:23:07,840
for enjoying my spouse.

328
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:09,890
Ow...

329
00:23:16,360 --> 00:23:18,510
I...I think we should dig in.

330
00:23:19,020 --> 00:23:20,340
Sarm, take a seat.

331
00:23:20,360 --> 00:23:21,220
Okay.

332
00:23:21,330 --> 00:23:22,490
Sure thing.

333
00:23:25,330 --> 00:23:26,330
Thank you.

334
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:38,930
I have a meeting with Ms. Vibhavadi at noon.

335
00:23:45,010 --> 00:23:46,930
You never have time for me.

336
00:23:49,080 --> 00:23:51,100
Oh, Sarm...

337
00:23:51,130 --> 00:23:52,740
It is not like that.

338
00:23:53,020 --> 00:23:53,650
I mean,

339
00:23:54,130 --> 00:23:56,410
you should try the stew.

340
00:23:56,490 --> 00:23:58,330
I made it myself.

341
00:23:58,470 --> 00:24:00,530
Whoa, five-spice stew with braised pork.

342
00:24:00,550 --> 00:24:02,120
Really? You made it yourself?

343
00:24:02,300 --> 00:24:03,630
Oh, is there a yogurt drink?

344
00:24:03,650 --> 00:24:04,900
Do we have any?

345
00:24:07,230 --> 00:24:08,490
You do not get to to have it today.

346
00:24:08,600 --> 00:24:10,490
Your sugar intake is already too high.

347
00:24:11,360 --> 00:24:12,360
Fine...

348
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:14,420
Whatever my spouse says.

349
00:24:15,130 --> 00:24:16,130
Good boy.

350
00:24:17,100 --> 00:24:18,550
Your cheeks are way sweeter anyway.

351
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:21,250
One more time.

352
00:24:24,830 --> 00:24:25,830
One more...

353
00:24:27,750 --> 00:24:29,920
By the way, my fists

354
00:24:30,810 --> 00:24:32,430
are second to none.

355
00:24:32,450 --> 00:24:33,740
Oh...

356
00:24:33,760 --> 00:24:34,760
Want some?

357
00:24:39,430 --> 00:24:40,430
I prefer this.

358
00:24:40,930 --> 00:24:42,210
It doesn't hurt either.

359
00:24:49,130 --> 00:24:51,050
We might as well skip this meal.

360
00:24:53,490 --> 00:24:54,490
Just a little more.

361
00:24:56,940 --> 00:24:58,930
We are in a dining room,

362
00:24:59,310 --> 00:25:00,650
not a battlefield.

363
00:25:01,020 --> 00:25:02,370
But with you,

364
00:25:02,630 --> 00:25:03,630
wherever you are,

365
00:25:03,650 --> 00:25:05,200
it's a "battlefield of love."

366
00:25:08,230 --> 00:25:10,270
Did you come up with that yourself

367
00:25:10,290 --> 00:25:12,140
or did you take it from a series?

368
00:25:12,270 --> 00:25:13,120
I came up with it myself.

369
00:25:13,750 --> 00:25:14,440
That's because

370
00:25:14,460 --> 00:25:15,920
the inspiration behind that phrase is you.

371
00:25:25,970 --> 00:25:26,970
- Let me have you one more time.
- Whoa...

372
00:25:29,250 --> 00:25:30,000
Oh!

373
00:25:30,220 --> 00:25:31,750
The food is getting cold at this point.

374
00:25:31,770 --> 00:25:32,330
Huh?

375
00:25:32,350 --> 00:25:33,740
- We can eat it later if we want to.
- At this point...

376
00:25:49,890 --> 00:25:50,890
Hey.

377
00:25:51,410 --> 00:25:52,720
Don't overwork yourself, okay?

378
00:25:53,110 --> 00:25:54,640
Call me if you're tired.

379
00:25:54,770 --> 00:25:55,830
Understood?

380
00:25:56,470 --> 00:25:57,550
Right.

381
00:25:57,580 --> 00:26:00,600
I have my personal consultant.

382
00:26:00,620 --> 00:26:01,750
Of course.

383
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:03,000
It's me,

384
00:26:03,020 --> 00:26:04,380
the spouse of the year,

385
00:26:05,110 --> 00:26:05,750
right?

386
00:26:06,190 --> 00:26:08,230
You are claiming the title yourself,
are you not?

387
00:26:18,230 --> 00:26:18,840
Hey.

388
00:26:30,530 --> 00:26:31,530
Thank you

389
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:34,240
for moving in with me completely.

390
00:26:36,830 --> 00:26:39,450
Your house is also mine.

391
00:26:41,240 --> 00:26:42,130
Bye-bye.

392
00:26:43,530 --> 00:26:44,450
Kiss, kiss.

393
00:26:45,630 --> 00:26:46,630
I will be going now.

394
00:26:46,930 --> 00:26:48,020
- Bye-bye.
- Bye-bye.

395
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:50,710
- Bye-bye.
- Bye-bye.

396
00:26:54,430 --> 00:26:55,050
Little Jam,

397
00:26:58,730 --> 00:26:59,500
I love you.

398
00:27:01,710 --> 00:27:03,340
- I love you, too.
- Bye-bye.

399
00:27:03,730 --> 00:27:04,560
Bye-bye.

400
00:27:04,580 --> 00:27:05,810
Do miss me, okay?

401
00:27:06,220 --> 00:27:07,730
All the time.

402
00:27:09,690 --> 00:27:10,910
Here's a kiss.

403
00:27:10,940 --> 00:27:11,540
Mwah, mwah.

404
00:27:13,140 --> 00:27:14,140
Mwah, mwah.

405
00:27:16,100 --> 00:27:17,100
Love you.

406
00:27:18,050 --> 00:27:18,880
Alright.

407
00:27:32,670 --> 00:27:33,610
I'm going to kiss a puppy,

408
00:27:33,630 --> 00:27:34,530
a kitten,

409
00:27:34,550 --> 00:27:35,240
and even a starfish.

410
00:27:35,260 --> 00:27:36,010
Mwah, mwah.

411
00:27:36,030 --> 00:27:38,300
♫Kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss♫

412
00:27:38,320 --> 00:27:40,120
♫This kiss is for you♫

413
00:27:40,140 --> 00:27:42,620
♫Ju Bu Ju Bu Ju Bu Jub♫

414
00:28:04,730 --> 00:28:06,210
Ow, this is killing me.

415
00:28:12,450 --> 00:28:13,340
Alright...

416
00:28:13,630 --> 00:28:14,630
Come here.

417
00:28:14,650 --> 00:28:16,230
Take a seat, Jam.

418
00:28:17,020 --> 00:28:17,920
I'll give you a massage.

419
00:28:25,860 --> 00:28:27,450
Where are you feeling sore?

420
00:28:29,830 --> 00:28:30,830
Here.

421
00:28:32,220 --> 00:28:33,040
Here?

422
00:28:41,030 --> 00:28:42,340
So good...

423
00:28:48,050 --> 00:28:49,520
Actually,

424
00:28:49,690 --> 00:28:51,820
hugging you already makes me feel better.

425
00:28:52,050 --> 00:28:53,050
Oh...

426
00:28:54,670 --> 00:28:56,930
So are you tired or feeling sore?

427
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:01,760
I want my spouse

428
00:29:01,780 --> 00:29:03,320
to live comfortably.

429
00:29:06,280 --> 00:29:08,820
I actually want you to take it easy on your work.

430
00:29:10,490 --> 00:29:13,160
I do not like being unoccupied.

431
00:29:16,740 --> 00:29:17,740
If so,

432
00:29:18,410 --> 00:29:20,360
we should have an eye-to-eye conversation.

433
00:29:23,430 --> 00:29:25,630
Can we instead change it to

434
00:29:26,190 --> 00:29:28,130
a your-hand-on-my-shoulder conversation?

435
00:29:29,420 --> 00:29:30,370
Oh,

436
00:29:30,390 --> 00:29:31,480
you want your body to feel good, no?

437
00:29:33,220 --> 00:29:34,210
Oh...

438
00:29:35,610 --> 00:29:37,840
Of course, it is you who are
giving me the massage.

439
00:29:41,530 --> 00:29:42,830
I'm serious, though.

440
00:29:45,540 --> 00:29:46,840
Maybe you have...

441
00:29:46,870 --> 00:29:47,950
actually been overworking.

442
00:29:49,130 --> 00:29:52,020
But things are going well.

443
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:57,640
If that's the case,

444
00:29:58,070 --> 00:29:59,070
how about this?

445
00:30:00,160 --> 00:30:01,410
On weekdays,

446
00:30:01,830 --> 00:30:03,520
work as much as you like,

447
00:30:03,850 --> 00:30:05,130
but on the weekends,

448
00:30:05,600 --> 00:30:07,430
consider spending time with your family.

449
00:30:10,620 --> 00:30:11,580
Would it be a good idea?

450
00:30:12,620 --> 00:30:13,720
Of course.

451
00:30:14,410 --> 00:30:17,600
Do you know that your extremely adorable,

452
00:30:17,730 --> 00:30:18,590
handsome,

453
00:30:18,620 --> 00:30:19,930
and perfect spouse

454
00:30:21,560 --> 00:30:23,150
is waiting to do activities together?

455
00:30:31,020 --> 00:30:32,650
What activities?

456
00:30:32,830 --> 00:30:36,000
I have already tried all of the rides
at Adisuan Farm.

457
00:30:36,250 --> 00:30:37,250
Oh.

458
00:30:37,320 --> 00:30:38,860
I've got so many games for you to play,

459
00:30:38,960 --> 00:30:40,340
like

460
00:30:40,530 --> 00:30:41,530
waking up a big worm,

461
00:30:42,520 --> 00:30:43,690
milking a so-called cow,

462
00:30:43,990 --> 00:30:44,930
or,

463
00:30:45,590 --> 00:30:46,880
kneading some bouncy buns.

464
00:30:48,150 --> 00:30:49,940
I've still got so much more.

465
00:30:51,770 --> 00:30:53,060
You're too obsessed, Sarm.

466
00:30:53,270 --> 00:30:54,090
What?

467
00:30:54,240 --> 00:30:56,120
I just want to have you. That's all.

468
00:30:56,270 --> 00:30:56,860
I want to have you

469
00:30:56,940 --> 00:30:59,140
day and night.

470
00:31:02,370 --> 00:31:05,290
We were just hugging each other
to sleep last night.

471
00:31:05,340 --> 00:31:06,190
Mm.

472
00:31:07,210 --> 00:31:08,720
Last night is now a past.

473
00:31:08,740 --> 00:31:10,030
What matters is tonight.

474
00:31:16,670 --> 00:31:17,740
I think...

475
00:31:19,280 --> 00:31:21,430
we should save our hugs for tomorrow morning

476
00:31:22,460 --> 00:31:24,250
before heading to work.

477
00:31:24,730 --> 00:31:25,900
It feels exciting that way.

478
00:31:27,880 --> 00:31:28,810
If that's the case,

479
00:31:30,120 --> 00:31:31,690
can I kiss you right now

480
00:31:31,950 --> 00:31:33,030
at least one time?

481
00:31:34,670 --> 00:31:35,670
Please?

482
00:32:19,020 --> 00:32:20,020
Shall we hit the shower?

483
00:32:25,500 --> 00:32:27,420
Do you want to shower first

484
00:32:28,420 --> 00:32:30,550
or should I go first?

485
00:32:31,030 --> 00:32:32,640
You're supposed to ask

486
00:32:32,930 --> 00:32:35,220
if we want to take a rain shower

487
00:32:35,240 --> 00:32:37,120
or take a warm bath.

488
00:32:37,330 --> 00:32:38,400
That should be the question.

489
00:32:38,550 --> 00:32:40,560
Who says I am going to shower with you?

490
00:32:40,700 --> 00:32:41,590
Come on, Little Jam.

491
00:32:41,610 --> 00:32:42,850
You are the only one imagining it.

492
00:32:43,770 --> 00:32:45,130
I'm telling you that right now.

493
00:32:45,530 --> 00:32:46,940
Sarm.

494
00:32:48,950 --> 00:32:51,320
Let me take care of you tonight,

495
00:32:51,630 --> 00:32:52,700
okay?

496
00:32:53,890 --> 00:32:54,640
Mm.

497
00:33:34,570 --> 00:33:36,030
Why are you staring at me so much?

498
00:33:36,730 --> 00:33:37,730
What?

499
00:33:38,340 --> 00:33:40,030
Why are you this adorable, then?

500
00:33:40,400 --> 00:33:41,760
Little Jam.

501
00:33:42,460 --> 00:33:44,250
Do you love me, though?

502
00:33:45,430 --> 00:33:46,350
I do.

503
00:33:47,550 --> 00:33:48,930
You're more than love to me.

504
00:33:52,270 --> 00:33:53,480
What about you?

505
00:33:53,530 --> 00:33:54,830
Do you love me?

506
00:34:07,260 --> 00:34:09,130
I also love you.

507
00:34:11,659 --> 00:34:12,659
I'm sorry?

508
00:34:12,739 --> 00:34:13,739
Didn't catch that.

509
00:34:14,530 --> 00:34:15,530
What did you say?

510
00:34:16,239 --> 00:34:18,760
I said, "I love you," alright?

511
00:34:18,780 --> 00:34:21,440
Oh, you're so sweet, my good boy.

512
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:23,170
Listen.

513
00:34:23,190 --> 00:34:24,909
From this day onward,

514
00:34:25,219 --> 00:34:26,219
there won't be a day

515
00:34:26,239 --> 00:34:27,650
that I don't love you.

516
00:34:48,929 --> 00:34:50,060
How about a session before the shower?

517
00:36:56,470 --> 00:36:57,690
Sarm...

518
00:36:58,020 --> 00:36:59,020
Sarm...

519
00:38:25,740 --> 00:38:26,840
What are you watching?

520
00:38:27,540 --> 00:38:28,900
Sarm.

521
00:38:29,620 --> 00:38:32,040
Look at this YouTuber eating a durian.

522
00:38:32,320 --> 00:38:33,880
- It looks so tasty.
- Whoa...

523
00:38:34,450 --> 00:38:35,840
You want a durian?

524
00:38:35,930 --> 00:38:37,130
Mm!

525
00:38:37,750 --> 00:38:40,540
I want it!

526
00:38:40,910 --> 00:38:42,050
If you do,

527
00:38:42,070 --> 00:38:43,350
what do you have to do first?

528
00:38:49,750 --> 00:38:50,520
Refreshing.

529
00:38:50,660 --> 00:38:51,430
Sure.

530
00:38:51,650 --> 00:38:52,650
I'll deliver.

531
00:38:56,430 --> 00:38:57,430
New and Jiew,

532
00:38:57,830 --> 00:38:59,250
durian!

533
00:39:00,460 --> 00:39:01,220
New and Jiew.

534
00:39:04,760 --> 00:39:06,290
Whoa...

535
00:39:07,780 --> 00:39:08,900
Thank you, New and Jiew.

536
00:39:09,040 --> 00:39:10,130
Oh...

537
00:39:10,760 --> 00:39:12,420
You are amazing, Sarm.

538
00:39:12,440 --> 00:39:13,210
Of course,

539
00:39:13,390 --> 00:39:15,810
there's nothing that your spouse cannot do.

540
00:39:16,140 --> 00:39:17,090
Let me just tell you that

541
00:39:17,110 --> 00:39:18,210
I can do everything

542
00:39:18,230 --> 00:39:19,520
under the sun.

543
00:39:22,370 --> 00:39:24,510
You are just too much!

544
00:39:26,350 --> 00:39:27,350
By the way...

545
00:39:28,420 --> 00:39:29,770
do you know how to open a durian?

546
00:39:30,640 --> 00:39:31,640
When it comes to this,

547
00:39:31,920 --> 00:39:32,830
don't worry.

548
00:39:33,600 --> 00:39:34,440
New and Jiew.

549
00:39:36,040 --> 00:39:36,960
Whoa...

550
00:39:39,280 --> 00:39:40,410
It won't take long.

551
00:39:41,040 --> 00:39:42,760
I cannot wait.

552
00:39:43,330 --> 00:39:44,330
New and Jiew.

553
00:39:46,650 --> 00:39:47,810
Thank you very much.

554
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:51,430
Looks just as tasty as the one in the video.

555
00:39:51,450 --> 00:39:52,320
Of course.

556
00:39:52,340 --> 00:39:53,950
This durian has a great shape

557
00:39:53,970 --> 00:39:54,920
and a beautiful color

558
00:39:54,950 --> 00:39:56,050
and it is perfectly formed.

559
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:02,820
Another bite?

560
00:40:03,130 --> 00:40:03,840
Mm.

561
00:40:07,180 --> 00:40:08,340
That's better.

562
00:40:08,980 --> 00:40:09,740
Is it sweet?

563
00:40:10,410 --> 00:40:11,330
Hm.

564
00:40:12,250 --> 00:40:13,830
It is so tasty.

565
00:40:14,530 --> 00:40:16,480
I want to have it every day.

566
00:40:16,860 --> 00:40:17,860
You can,

567
00:40:17,880 --> 00:40:19,440
but you have to exercise, too.

568
00:40:20,780 --> 00:40:22,430
Can I exercise later?

569
00:40:22,750 --> 00:40:23,840
I will do it later.

570
00:40:23,960 --> 00:40:24,830
Sure.

571
